  "date": "2026-08-16",
  "purpose": "Build a real offline per-model policy pipeline (fingerprint -> sensitivity profile -> mixed-layout policy) and measure it head-to-head against the product's already-shipped, unmodified whole-cache adaptive Q8/Q5 policy -- not just against naive layouts as in 11C -- across calibration-set sizes, held-out prompts, and both tested models.",
  "literal_verdict": "MODEL_SPECIFIC_POLICY_WORKS_BUT_NO_ADAPTIVE_ADVANTAGE",
  "verdict_summary": "The full offline pipeline is real, safe, reproducible (byte-identical profiles across repeated runs), and generalizes across calibration sizes, held-out prompts, and both tested models -- not a fragile or backend-limited result. But measured head-to-head against the shipped, unmodified whole-cache adaptive policy, profile-based mixed KV does not win in the regime that matters most in practice: in comfortable memory (where adaptive resolves to whole-cache Q8), adaptive clearly beats mixed KV on quality at similar byte cost. Mixed KV's one genuine advantage -- filling the quality gap between whole-cache Q5 and Q8 -- only matters in the narrower case where adaptive would otherwise be forced down to whole-cache Q5 by memory pressure, which this phase did not reproduce at an apples-to-apples boundary (left to Phase 11E). The real memory-pressure margin at the one boundary tested was also found to be tighter than the pure byte-budget policy math suggested -- a real caveat on how far this mechanism could be pushed.",
  "verdict_source": "results/canonical/summary.json: decision_gate.verdict, decision_gate.rationale (literal source fields, not synthesized)",
  "productized": false,
  "product_pr": null,
  "product_commit": null,
  "reproducibility": "PARTIALLY_REPRODUCIBLE",
  "hardware": "Real GTX 1650 (Vulkan backend) and same host's CPU",
  "models": [
    "SmolLM2-135M-Instruct-f16",
    "SmolLM2-360M-Instruct-f16"
  ],
  "llama_cpp_pin": "c0bc8591e8815c63cb01dd3f051a8b0df02501c9",
  "follow_up": "The one open question this phase explicitly left (does mixed KV beat whole-cache Q5, specifically, at the memory-pressure boundary where adaptive is forced down to Q5) directly set up Phase 11E's constrained, apples-to-apples comparison at exactly that boundary. Source HEAD 96b93b1de8acd35cce50055b91ce2ae8d6246039.",
